WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.234
-Our next guest is

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.269
a Grammy-nominated
singer and songwriter

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.571
whose new single, "Brrr,"
is out now.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.274
Please welcome to the show,
Kim Petras, everybody!

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:11.277
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:28.060 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.395
-Welcome to the show, Kim!

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.730
Are you well?
-Thank you!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.598
Yeah, I'm so excited to be here.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:34.400
-I was so excited to see you
on Saturday.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.002
You made your "SNL" debut,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.504
and I think it's always
a little nerve-wracking

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.007
to appear on "SNL"
for the first time.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.710
You had sort of
a higher bar of entry

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.045
than anyone I've ever seen,
because you were sort of

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.848
hiding under Sam's dress
and then revealed.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.484
-Yeah.
It was a moment, for sure.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.086
I was under there for
a long time.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.121
-Yeah.
-So it was very well-rehearsed.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:59.024
-And I've got to imagine it's
not super cool and breezy.

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:00.359
-Not at all.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.227
-Nope. It was very hot.

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:03.429
I was, like, sweating.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.564
And also, Sam was moving a lot,
so I was like --

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.333
I don't know if you guys know
the little Kim dance,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.602
but I was like --

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.870
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.338
You know, I was just
trying to, like --

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.373
because I had to hold it,
because otherwise,

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.409
I would get these crazy flyaways
and everyone would be like,

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.845
"She had flyaways last time,"
so it was just like, yeah.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.847
I just had to dodge with Sam.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.615
But worth it.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.450
-Someone on TikTok predicted it,
but other than that,

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.584
it was a surprise.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:27.486
-Someone predicted you'd
be under the dress?

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.622
-Yes, there's a TikTok
that's like,

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.290
"Oh, I bet she's
under the dress,"

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.125
and then they all
scream and jump up.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.827
It's good!

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.564
-You also got to go to
the afterparty.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:40.032
Here you are with the
wonderful host of the evening,

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:41.033
Aubrey Plaza.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.335
-Aubrey! I'm such a fan.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:46.105
-This is a big deal. Madonna!

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.074
Now, had you ever met
Madonna before?

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:53.646
-Um, I met her briefly
at Pride years ago,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.581
but not like this.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:59.452
We talked and I was, like,
really obliterated drunk

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.553
and I was just like,
"You're my queen!"

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:03.723
And it was the afterparty
and she just showed up.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:06.024
I'm sure she thinks I'm crazy.

00:02:06.024 --> 00:02:07.093
But yeah, I was like,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.394
"You are the blueprint
for everybody

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.562
and you need to know this!

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:10.963
And this album means
so much to me

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.064
and 'Confessions
on the Dance Floor'

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:13.132
was the best album ever."

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.466
I was just, like, going ham,

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.135
and then she was like,
"You want to take a picture?"

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.170
She was like, "Mm-hmm."

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.907
-By the way,
there's nothing better

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.941
than when a celebrity
clocks the moment

00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:24.944
and is like, "I'm gonna
ask you to stop talking."

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.846
-Yeah.
-And we're gonna get

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.747
the picture that you're gonna
want from this moment, right?

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:30.883
-Yeah, no, totally, because
I wouldn't have gotten one.

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.518
I was like, way too scared.
-Is this the moment after?

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:36.189
-Yes! [ Laughs ]

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.258
-She was just like, it felt like

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.792
she was my only friend
when I was a kid.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.994
I listened to her music!

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.697
It went on for, like,
10 minutes.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.432
I was crying my makeup off.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.033
-Oh, my God. What a night.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.536
First you're under a dress,
then you meet Madonna.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:51.737
There's a lot going on.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.172
-It's a Tuesday for me.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.406
-Yeah.

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.375
-I think you and I live
very different lives.

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.111
Another difference,

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.312
I've never been nominated
for a Grammy.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.613
You got nominated for
a Grammy this year.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.483
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:08.020
-What was the moment like
where you got to find out?

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.722
-My team yelled at me
from downstairs

00:03:10.722 --> 00:03:12.758
and just, like,
came into my room

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.026
and I was just, like,
getting ready and I was like,

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.329
"What?" and yeah,
they were just like,

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.530
"You're nominated for a Grammy,"

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.599
and we all started
crying and jumping

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.066
and doing the things you do,

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:22.235
so yeah, it's crazy.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.069
I can't believe it.
-Seems like you've had

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.403
a lot of good cries recently.

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:25.771
I think it's a very nice sign.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.439
-Yeah, I cry a lot.

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:28.908
-Yeah, that's alright.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.977
I men, if you're crying for
getting nominated for a Grammy,

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.411
like, let the tears flow, right?

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.113
-Yeah, for sure.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.581
-Good cries. Good cries.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:40.586
-You and Sam, you got nominated
for the song that was your duet,

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.155
and you also set sort of a --

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:46.091
It was a historical precedent
for LGBTQ representation

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:47.894
at the Grammys, so
congratulations on that as well.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:51.664
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.166
-Thanks, guys.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:56.502
Yeah, I mean, it's so crazy.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:04:00.873
I feel like gay clubs raised me
and pop music.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:04.710
No one loves pop music
more than gay clubs,

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:09.115
and honestly, I owe everything
I have to the gays in Bushwick.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:12.619
You guys, honestly, I used to

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:16.122
perform on tables in bars
and whatever,

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.590
and now I'm nominated
for a Grammy.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.425
It's so crazy,
because those were always

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.461
the places where I just, like,
felt like I belonged in there,

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:25.765
where like, pop music
and fun music is celebrated

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.334
like it has won
a bunch of Grammys.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:32.771
So it's crazy that Sam and I
kind of did this club song

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:35.641
and it got nominated
for a Grammy.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:38.477
And it's a very gay song,
so thank you, Grammys.

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:41.280
I really appreciate it.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.648
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:46.185
-Sam must be an incredible
person to collaborate with,

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:51.024
but I also a video of you
singing with your dog.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.859
-Yeah.
-Your dog Karl, is that right?

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:56.328
-Karl, "Carl" with a K.
-Okay, Karl with a K.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:59.965
And now we have a video of you
singing and Karl joining you.

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:01.901
Did this happen naturally
the first time?

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.836
Did Karl just start singing
along with you?

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:07.072
-Yeah, it kind of
happened right away.

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:10.443
Whenever I warm up,
he sits next to me,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:14.279
on the chair next to me
and sings with me,

00:05:14.279 --> 00:05:16.381
and he's really good.

00:05:16.381 --> 00:05:18.083
He's getting better,
and I'm --

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.251
-But this isn't a --

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:20.386
You didn't go to
the pet store and say,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.820
"Obviously, I'd love a dog
that could sing."

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.989
-No, of course I didn't.
-Okay, okay. Gotcha.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:26.392
-Yeah, and I have
two other dogs,

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:30.129
so I was not expecting
such a brilliant voice

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.964
to come out of that guy.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:35.868
-Do the other dogs kind of
think Karl's a lot?

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.103
Are they like, ugh?
-Yeah.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:39.371
They're like,
"There he goes again.

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:42.742
All the attention."
They're mad in the corner.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.210
-Let's see the
attention-grabbing

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.210
Karl the dog.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:50.649
-[ Singing scales ]

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:53.119
-[ Howling in tune ]

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.520
-[ Laughs ] Aww.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.389
-[ Singing scales ]

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.590
-[ Howling ]

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.327
[ Laughing ]
-Pretty amazing!

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.662
[ Applause ]

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:06.165
Pretty impressive.
-That's Karl.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.233
He's a star.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:10.469
Stealing my shine.
Stop it, Karl!

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:11.937
-This is a true story.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:15.541
You are a huge fan of our other
guest tonight, Hilary Duff.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.342
-Yes.
-What is your history

00:06:17.342 --> 00:06:19.144
with Hilary Duff as a fan?

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:22.848
-Well, "Metamorphosis"
shaped me as a person.

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:25.218
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:28.053
I mean, honestly,
"Lizzie McGuire"

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:30.822
was like, my life
when I was a kid.

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:32.257
I'm obsessed with her.

00:06:32.257 --> 00:06:33.493
I'm obsessed with her concerts,

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:35.694
and I was like,
shrieking and freaking out

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:37.029
when I just met her backstage.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.131
It's been so crazy
meeting all these legends,

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.067
and I just, like,
"Okay, here we go.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.868
Just cry again, freak out,
you know."

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.071
But yeah, she just, like,

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:47.473
is so iconic,
and her music is so good.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.942
And she really doesn't get
the credit that she deserves.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:52.244
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:53.845
You know?
-Let's get her out here

00:06:53.845 --> 00:06:55.748
and fix that.
-Pop star.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.884
-I'm very happy about this
and I want to thank you

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.019
for sticking around.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:01.654
You're gonna do your new song,
"Brrr."

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.122
Am I saying that...?
Is that a good...?

00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:05.892
That's alright? I can...?
-Yeah, no. That's good.

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:06.825
It's not [Rolling R's] "Brrrrr."

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:08.094
-Okay, good.
-Yeah.

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:10.596
-It's "brr"? Alright, great.
Thank you very much.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.732
And you've also had
a song called "Icy."

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:16.802
Is this sort of winter theme
something that is true to you?

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.538
-Yeah, I mean, I'm from Germany,
so it's cold there.

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:23.108
And I just feel like
the whole kind of like,

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:27.880
industrial feel of Germany
just offers itself to ice.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.916
So all my fans keep making memes
of, like, Elsa twerking,

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:32.985
and I really appreciate it.
-Alright, great.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.487
-That's honestly what
I want to give, you know?

00:07:35.487 --> 00:07:36.923
A video of Elsa twerking.

00:07:36.923 --> 00:07:38.724
So yeah, they're connected.

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:42.127
I have an ice block in my show,
so yeah.

00:07:42.127 --> 00:07:43.996
More ice songs.
-There you go. More ice songs.

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.832
Well, I think probably you were
thinking about that ice block

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:48.000
when you were under Sam's dress.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.269
You were like,
could have used that today.

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.238
-I could have really
used that then.

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:53.972
It wasn't there.

00:07:53.972 --> 00:07:55.274
-Your fans have an album
to look forward to.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.442
Tour as well? Are you gonna go
on the road in 2023?

00:07:57.442 --> 00:08:01.180
-Yes, summer. So excited.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.583
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.351
Yeah, and it's been awhile.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:07.386
It was like, before the pandemic
that I toured last.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.154
-Oh, well, they'll be very, very
happy to see you.

00:08:09.154 --> 00:08:11.691
-Thank God. Thank God.
-Alright.

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:13.792
I'm very excited to see you
in a few minutes.

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:16.028
You guys, that's Kim Petras.
Give it up!

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:19.598
We'll be right back with
her debut TV performance

00:08:19.598 --> 00:08:21.734
of her new single, "Brrr."

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.536
-Brr!
-Brr! [Rolling R's]

